  "attribution_note": "Classical equilateral triangular tiling, proper cube symmetries and Cartesian layer composition. No finite published donor packing. PingYou Ltd supplies the finite whole-strip assemblies and complete certificates.",
  "construction": {
   "name": "complete_triangular_strips_in_mixed_axis_layers",
   "proof": "ALTERNATING WHOLE-TRIANGLE STRIP RETURN\n\nThe ordinary bounding cell loses half its area for an equilateral triangle.\nRecover that area by a physical marked return before attempting a metric\nrealization. Put a=1/sqrt(3). The canonical unit-edge triangle has vertices\n(a,0),(-a/2,1/2),(-a/2,-1/2). For index t>=0, use its identity frame when\nt is even and its half-turn about z when t is odd. Put its center at\n((t mod 2)*a/2,t/2,0). Consecutive triangles share a complete oblique edge;\ntheir interiors lie on opposite sides of that edge. Nonconsecutive\ntriangles have disjoint y interiors except possible shared boundary.\nExtruding each complete triangle through the same prism height L keeps\nthe same nonoverlap and all whole-owner identities.\n\nA strip of m such prisms lies in the exact rectangle\n[-a/2,a] by [-1/2,m/2], extruded through [-L/2,L/2]. Its dimensions are\nsqrt(3)/2, (m+1)/2, L. Its midpoint is (a/4,(m-1)/4,0).\nThe additional half-unit of height is the retained pair of end costs;\nit may not be discarded by an infinite-strip density argument.\n\nPut complete strips in disjoint rectangular grid cells using these exact\ndimensions. A grid A by B by C fits in the common cube of side\nmax(A*sqrt(3)/2,B*(m+1)/2,C*L), and contains A*B*C*m complete prisms.\nKeep an explicitly indexed subset of N whole owners. This is a complete\nfinite return, not a marginal planar capacity statement.\n\nThe source is the classical equilateral triangular tiling and Cartesian\ncomposition. PingYou Ltd supplies the finite strip/grid assemblies and\ntheir certificates, without claiming the classical tiling as new. The\nzero-gain ordinary-length branch and every tested finite strip length\nremain useful controls. Native witnesses round the prescribed centers,\napply one common tiny outward dilation, retain the exact two half-turn\nquaternions, and are checked on every actual host wall and owner pair.\n\nCOMPLETE TRIANGULAR STRIPS IN MIXED-AXIS LAYERS\n\nUse the complete m-owner source in TRIANGLE_STRIP_PROOF.txt as one module.\nIts box dimensions are sqrt(3)/2, (m+1)/2, L; the half-unit end cost stays\nin every copy. Apply only the identity and the two fixed cyclic coordinate\nrotations. A layer whose vertical intrinsic dimension is dk contains a\nrectangular grid of complete modules with the other two dimensions.\n\nFor a common transverse side S and layer word (L0,L1,L2), the number of\nwhole prism owners is m times the sum over k of\nLk*floor(S/di)*floor(S/dj), where {i,j,k}={0,1,2}. The actual total layer\nheight is L0*d0+L1*d1+L2*d2. The common enclosing cube has side the maximum\nof S and this height. Layers are centered as one stack; the modules in\neach layer share the same transverse cube walls. No layer or module has\nan independent enclosing scale.\n\nEvery module's internal alternating owners and source frames are carried\nthrough its common cyclic rotation. Between modules the complete boxes\nseparate; inside each module the marked whole-triangle return supplies\nseparation. Deleting a named owner is permitted only after retaining the\nfull parent module and the complete assembly decoder. All native centers\nreceive one common outward dilation, with a matching host dilation; every\nactual owner pair and host wall is then checked exactly.\n",
